    "['term [parameter2] from route-filter [parameter3]/[parameter4] [parameter5]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-map advertise-networks permit 1', 'parent_command': ['route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]'], 'root': 'route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nroute-map advertise-networks permit 1\\n match ip address prefix-list exact-route\\nip prefix-list exact-route permit 22.22.22.22/32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper's `policy-statement` with `route-filter` is translated to Cisco's `route-map` with `prefix-list`\\n- The `exact` match in Juniper becomes an exact prefix match in Cisco (specified by the /32 mask)\\n- The term number (1) is preserved in the route-map sequence number\\n- Cisco requires separate creation of the prefix-list that's referenced in the route-map\", 'trans_template': 'route-map advertise-networks permit 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'match ip address prefix-list exact-route', 'parent_command': ['route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]'], 'root': 'route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nroute-map advertise-networks permit 1\\n match ip address prefix-list exact-route\\nip prefix-list exact-route permit 22.22.22.22/32\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper's `policy-statement` with `route-filter` is translated to Cisco's `route-map` with `prefix-list`\\n- The `exact` match in Juniper becomes an exact prefix match in Cisco (specified by the /32 mask)\\n- The term number (1) is preserved in the route-map sequence number\\n- Cisco requires separate creation of the prefix-list that's referenced in the route-map\", 'trans_template': 'match ip address prefix-list exact-route'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip prefix-list exact-route permit 22.22.22.22/32', 'parent_command': ['route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]'], 'root': 'route-map [parameter1] [parameter2] [parameter3]', 'source': 'llm'